{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-v4-medium-196-qwen3.8-27b-xhigh-yarn1m-full200-2026-09-22","prediction_set_name":"qwen3.8-27b-xhigh-yarn1m-full200-2026-09-22","paper_id":"2504.01938","judge_input_sha256":"27f2158dd3ae9e1a6656851e06b72c3f700dec16a2fba44a273beb3e2dcde6b5","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2504.01938:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2504.01938:I001:U001","2504.01938:I001:U002","2504.01938:I001:U004"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U002","ISSUE-001:U004","ISSUE-001:U009"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns misuse of a state-dependent random measure as an ordinary Poisson random measure, including invalid unconditional Poisson and independence claims. ISSUE-001 concerns transposed rate-matrix entries in a discrete-diffusion loss and does not diagnose the stochastic-integral construction.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2504.01938:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_operation_step_or_formula","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2504.01938:I002:U001","2504.01938:I002:U002","2504.01938:I002:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U003","ISSUE-002:U010"],"same_causal_subject":true,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"Both entries concern the Doob or h-transformed generator, but the gold defect is the arbitrary-lambda statement failing to preserve the path measure and conservativity, whereas ISSUE-002 diagnoses an incorrectly defined carré du champ and a resulting algebraic identity. These are distinct formulas and obligations.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2504.01938:I008","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-003","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2504.01938:I008:U001","2504.01938:I008:U002","2504.01938:I008:U003","2504.01938:I008:U007"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-003:U002","ISSUE-003:U003","ISSUE-003:U010"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the missing random endpoint ratio in a pathwise Radon–Nikodym density and the invalid pathwise use of Dynkin's formula. ISSUE-003 concerns a separate backward-simulation shortcut for jump-intensity integrals and does not identify the density or endpoint-factor defect.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}